Gameserver is full-fledged production level multiplayer game server.
Previous version supported loadbalancing (relay server) - see relay example.
Currently this functionality has been switched off temporarily (after moving into JMS compliant
messages relay package has to be updated).

For running server either use scripts or run server from command line having server.jar 
in CLASSPATH (it already contains both classes from this directory and necessary LJMS classes).

For currently supported arguments which can be passed to the applications during 
start just run "java Server -h" or "java Server -help" (one can change log directories, log files names, debug levels etc through arguments).

For simple client one can run whiteboard (whiteboard package/example). Real production
clients working with this server are not placed here.

